  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1156 PM CDT WED APR 15 2026\n\nThe upper-level pattern will slowly begin to break down over the \nnext 36-hours, as a deep trough and cold front begin to move east \nout of the central Plains. Rain chances will finally return to the \nforecast by late Saturday evening, as this cold front begins to \nwork into the region. While any rain at this point is welcomed, it\nwill hardly be the rainfall the region needs to make any sort of \nmeaningful impact on the ongoing drought. Most locations will \ngenerally see between a quarter and a half-inch of rainfall when \nits all said and done Sunday afternoon.\n\nTemperatures behind the cold front will drop some 15-20 degrees, \nwith afternoon highs on Sunday ranging in the upper-60s to low-70s. \nWith that being said, temperatures will quickly rebound as a subtle \nridge works back into the region. While this climb will be slow, \nafternoon highs should be back in the low-80s by Wednesday. \n\n/44/",
